Docker images Features
1. Lighweight 
    -> share resource efficiently
    -> as they use the host OS kernal instead running full OS
2. Layered Structure
    -> images are composed of multiplies read only layers. each layers represents a set of file sytem chnages like(Modificaiton, addition, deletion)
3. immutability
   -> one built they cannot be altered
4. portability 
5. versioning and tags
6. base image support
7. security Features
   -> images can include signed digest for authenticity verification, ensuring that the image has'nt been tempered with
   -> tools like DOCKER CONTENT TRUST(DCT) can be used to enforce singing plicies

Characteristics of Docker Images
1. File system snapshot
2. Union file system(UFS)
   -> docker uses a union file system to stack layers and preent them as single cohensive file system
3. Read only layers
   -> images are composed of read-only layers, while containers add a writeable layer on top for runtime chnages
4. Delarative configuration
5. OS and architecuture
6. Compact storage
   -> shared layer between image minimize storage usages and speed up downloads
7. Dependency isolation
   -> each image encapsulated its dependencies, ensuring no conflits between app. running on the same host
8. Stateless
   -> image are inherently Stateless
   -> persistent storages requires mounting volumes or using external storage solution
9.distribution format
  -> image are distributed as tarball files
10.identified hashes
  -> each images has a unique SHA-256 digest hash for identification/
